Clearcote optional Mac-host adapter: distinguish Windows ARM hosts from Mac ARM hosts

Why: Chromium150's Windows metadata import requests ARM64 Windows libraries whenever
host_cpu is arm64, including a Mac ARM64 host targeting Windows x64. Those libraries
are not the Mac host sysroot and are not used by the x64 target. Only a Windows ARM
host (or a genuine Windows ARM64 target) requires this additional Windows payload.
Windows-only Rust/system-allocator host variants are likewise created only on
Windows hosts; Mac host tools continue through the native Mac toolchain.
The unconditional, real x86/x64 metadata and nocompile checks remain enabled.

